Upstream: none found (GitLab search 2026-11-21).

Limitor's consume, data_consume and data_consume_hard returned the inner reader's buffer cut at
the limit, which the BufferedReader documentation allows (the returned buffer includes the
consumed data and may extend past it). This patch cuts it to the consumed amount instead, and
consume and data_consume_hard assert that the inner reader returned at least `amount` bytes. It
does not fix a known panic: self.limit + amount is the limit before the call and cannot overflow,
the slices stayed within the buffer, and a short buffer from the inner data_consume_hard, which
was passed on before and then failed the assert in BufferedReader::steal, now fails the new
assert. Callers see fewer bytes past the consumed data, so the patch changes behaviour; it is kept
as its own patch for that reason and has no test. 645k distinct crash inputs collected by fuzzing
the openpgp fuzz targets give the same panics with and without it (native x86_64 and i686 release
builds).

diff --git a/buffered-reader/src/limitor.rs b/buffered-reader/src/limitor.rs
index a700ae70..44effcf4 100644
--- a/buffered-reader/src/limitor.rs
+++ b/buffered-reader/src/limitor.rs
@@ -88,17 +88,20 @@ impl<T: BufferedReader<C>, C: fmt::Debug + Sync + Send> BufferedReader<C> for Li
         assert!(amount as u64 <= self.limit);
         self.limit -= amount as u64;
         let data = self.reader.consume(amount);
-        &data[..cmp::min(self.limit + amount as u64, data.len() as u64) as usize]
+        assert!(
+            data.len() >= amount,
+            "inner reader must return at least `amount` bytes from consume"
+        );
+        &data[..amount]
     }
 
     fn data_consume(&mut self, amount: usize) -> Result<&[u8], io::Error> {
         let amount = cmp::min(amount as u64, self.limit) as usize;
         let result = self.reader.data_consume(amount);
         if let Ok(buffer) = result {
-            let amount = cmp::min(amount, buffer.len());
-            self.limit -= amount as u64;
-            return Ok(&buffer[
-                ..cmp::min(buffer.len() as u64, self.limit + amount as u64) as usize]);
+            let consumed = cmp::min(amount, buffer.len());
+            self.limit -= consumed as u64;
+            return Ok(&buffer[..consumed]);
         }
         result
     }
@@ -109,10 +112,12 @@ impl<T: BufferedReader<C>, C: fmt::Debug + Sync + Send> BufferedReader<C> for Li
         }
         let result = self.reader.data_consume_hard(amount);
         if let Ok(buffer) = result {
-            let amount = cmp::min(amount, buffer.len());
+            assert!(
+                buffer.len() >= amount,
+                "inner reader must return at least `amount` bytes from data_consume_hard"
+            );
             self.limit -= amount as u64;
-            return Ok(&buffer[
-                ..cmp::min(buffer.len() as u64, self.limit + amount as u64) as usize]);
+            return Ok(&buffer[..amount]);
         }
         result
     }
